  m_text: "A decomposition reaction is a chemical reaction in which one compound
    breaks down into two or more simpler substances. In the thermal decomposition
    of calcium carbonate, heating causes calcium carbonate to form calcium oxide
    and carbon dioxide gas. The reaction is represented as CaCO3 \u2192 CaO + CO2.
    This is an example of decomposition caused by heat."
