  questions:
  - questionText: What happens during a decomposition reaction?
    options:
    - One compound breaks down into two or more simpler substances
    - Two elements always form one compound
    - One element replaces another element
    - Two compounds exchange their ions
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What happens to calcium carbonate when it is strongly heated?
    options:
    - It decomposes into calcium oxide and carbon dioxide
    - It forms calcium carbonate and oxygen
    - It changes only into carbon dioxide
    - It does not undergo a chemical change
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: Which gas is released when calcium carbonate decomposes on heating?
    options:
    - Carbon dioxide
    - Oxygen
    - Hydrogen
    - Nitrogen
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
  - questionText: What solid remains after the thermal decomposition of calcium carbonate?
    options:
    - Calcium oxide
    - Calcium chloride
    - Calcium sulfate
    - Calcium hydroxide
    correctAnswerIndex: 0
    questionVoice: {fileID: 0}
    correctAnswerVoice: {fileID: 0}
